  "mapping": {
    "authored_date": "2026-07-18",
    "deviation_notes": "Clean map to ground_targeted_circle + poison (crosswalk-mandated chaos->shadow+poison home); the hit-independent 'only the ground cloud matters' identity is native to a zone-occupancy DoT. Minor drift: PoE Caustic Arrow is a fixed-tick chaos DAMAGE-OVER-TIME cloud, while the engine `poison` ailment is stack-additive (cap 5-10); the DoT-cloud-vs-stacking-ailment nuance is smoothed by the mandated lane. Wither-totem chaos-taken amp routed as ailment-scaling debuff, noted.",
    "grade": "CLOSE",
    "kit_id": "poe1-caustic-arrow",
    "mapping_json": {
      "fidelity_notes": "The original ground-DoT bow archetype, TR's ancestor. ground_targeted_circle + poison ailment is the crosswalk-mandated home (chaos-poison -> shadow family + poison lane, §1/§2). The 'accuracy and crit are irrelevant; only the ground pool matters' identity is NATIVE to a ground_targeted_circle DoT that damages via zone-occupancy. Honest CLOSE-not-EXACT drift: PoE CA is a chaos DAMAGE-OVER-TIME cloud (a persistent-DoT debuff), whereas the engine `poison` ailment is a STACK-ADDITIVE ailment (cap 5-10 stacks per §2). The engine expresses 'caustic DoT' via the poison lane, but PoE CA's cloud is a fixed-tick ground-DoT, not a per-target stacking application — a nuance the poison-ailment mapping smooths. Wither totems (chaos-taken amp linked skill) route as an ailment-scaling support / curse-adjacent debuff, noted; PERSISTENCE_ENGINE_uptime for the maintain-the-DoT-uptime capstone.",
      "motion_frame": "kite-the-cloud DoT ranger: plant a caustic pool, walk enemies through it, layer Wither totems + curses; fire-and-forget, hit-independent",
      "option_c_substrate_flags": null,
      "resource_economy": {},
      "scaffold": {
        "chain_count": 2,
